Train-val accuracy gap:
  Train top-1 is ~57-61% due to MixUp/CutMix augmentation (expected to be low).
  Val top-1 is 88-91%. The apparent "gap" is an artifact of data augmentation --
  MixUp/CutMix makes training accuracy artificially low because labels are mixed
  probability distributions, but accuracy is measured against original hard labels.
  This is NOT overfitting in the traditional sense.

Calibration concern:
  Val loss is rising (1.19 -> 1.44) while val accuracy only dropped moderately
  (91.4% -> 87.9%). The model is becoming LESS CALIBRATED -- predictions are
  increasingly overconfident on wrong classes or underconfident on right classes.
  Label smoothing (0.1) adds ~0.1-0.15 to cross-entropy, so true CE is ~1.2-1.3.

LR schedule issue:
  LR is ramping UP through cosine warmup (1e-6 -> 7.86e-5 from E16-E25).
  Warmup = 3 epochs means E16-E18 were warmup. Since E19, LR has been increasing
  along the cosine schedule toward the peak. The degradation correlates with
  rising LR -- the model checkpoint was already well-trained (91% val) and the
  cosine schedule is pushing LR too high, destabilizing the fine-tuned weights.
  
  Expected behavior: LR will peak soon and then decay. Val accuracy should
  recover as LR decreases in the second half of training (epochs 30-60).
  Peak LR for this schedule = learning_rate (from config). The current trajectory
  suggests the model will likely recover best performance around epochs 40-50
  when LR drops back to low values.

